Subject: Semantic Anchor Catalogue P0 Slice5F SJS Review 2026-08-23

@ [review_uuid] 5916c8fd-b22a-4e0a-a5fc-641b5e2cab74

& [Situation]
  + Slice5E exposes exact candidate identities and anchors but intentionally leaves target selections null

& [Justification]
  + Slice6 needs an auditable supplied selection path while Cantor must not invent curator authority

& [Solution]
  + verify one externally supplied trust policy and Ed25519-signed selection against exact dossier bytes and emit a typed non-authoritative receipt

& [Delineation]
  + cryptographic signature verifies key possession and payload integrity
  + separately admitted policy provenance establishes whether that key has governance authority
  + synthetic fixture status proves mechanics only and cannot become a governed selection

& [Decision]
  + activate additive provider-free protocol forms verifier fixture binary tests and evidence only
